# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two reasons this file matters more than it looks:
#   1. Secrets. A stray .env in the build context ends up in the `builder` and `migrator`
#      layers via `COPY . .` and is then readable forever with `docker history` /
#      `docker save`, even though the runner stage never copies it.
#   2. Cache. node_modules is ~700 MB; shipping it as context invalidates the build cache
#      on every unrelated file-watcher touch and makes every build minutes slower.

# --- Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.yarn
.npm

# --- Secrets. Never in a layer. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
secrets/
**/*.secret

# --- VCS and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Build output: regenerated inside the image ---
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- Test artefacts ---
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.playwright
tests/**/__screenshots__

# --- Infra and docs: not needed to build the app, and changing the runbook must not
#     invalidate the image cache ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
infra
docs
backups
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
